{"id": "EUVD-2026-76527", "enisaUuid": "17140998-dc38-33e8-aea0-7d77f52f2de6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfs/ntfs3: bound page_lcns[] index by the log record\n\nThe copy_lcns loop and the redo shorten loop index page_lcns[] at j + i,\nwhere i runs up to the log record's lcns_follow. That count is checked only\nagainst the record's own length, not the target entry, so check_dp_table()\n(which validates the entry's lcns_follow) does not cover it: the copy_lcns\nentry may even be freshly allocated after that check, and find_dp() bounds j\nbut not i. A crafted record thus overflows page_lcns[] of an otherwise valid\nentry.\n\nAdd dp_range_ok() and reject, before each loop, any record whose run does\nnot fit the entry. These are the only two page_lcns[] accesses indexed by\nthe record rather than the entry, so together with the entry validation\nevery access is now bounded.\n\n[almaz.alexandrovich@paragon-software.com: original patch contained changes to the problem already handled, applied partly]", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:47", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/31fdd11f75da9823500168cecb07aa45130915a3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb742d1030864c0fe140666f639428ba4e90b2ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/61ca8cbbf68f77f25b699ed4358bd232f94ed43b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f4c1bc6d7331f344ffcea93c2a37badcbe15baa6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ccb94901f38a062034b56b43c774050b113758f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1135ebc225996b3ac1a295652b19a0a706737a6c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6f7b9dbdc1b7520206abce0049bdd143eb536e75"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89615", "GHSA-r33c-hmhm-vc95"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00cab8cc-08d0-3f10-a3ac-d4d519c8c5c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b46acd6a6a627d876898e1c84d3f84902264b445 <31fdd11f75da9823500168cecb07aa45130915a3"}, {"id": "0cf992cc-afd2-3aed-9cc7-4cd98aa8fb92", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b46acd6a6a627d876898e1c84d3f84902264b445 <f4c1bc6d7331f344ffcea93c2a37badcbe15baa6"}, {"id": "147b7939-d009-3d65-a13b-2577129bde3a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "1a0df70b-1919-3eaf-a996-9bbc6e327cf5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "44557318-125c-385f-9bba-91faec12c95d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b46acd6a6a627d876898e1c84d3f84902264b445 <bb742d1030864c0fe140666f639428ba4e90b2ca"}, {"id": "80831c54-6323-3c42-9724-d34dba7b42e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b46acd6a6a627d876898e1c84d3f84902264b445 <6f7b9dbdc1b7520206abce0049bdd143eb536e75"}, {"id": "808aa304-62d8-3447-8c62-f7d769fe4e3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b46acd6a6a627d876898e1c84d3f84902264b445 <7ccb94901f38a062034b56b43c774050b113758f"}, {"id": "a5c52ba9-4e08-3616-9349-efcd8cac659c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "b30318e7-1841-3f62-8349-0e5a866bb78e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "c167249f-ebe2-392d-a779-a2ad25fbe7f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "cd8a1d78-1e3e-33b8-b956-27db1cbab8bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "e1c40a24-fb86-3bc7-ac40-0b0fb2839bb2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b46acd6a6a627d876898e1c84d3f84902264b445 <61ca8cb